# Language: CalcLang
# Description: A functional calculator language
# Author: LFE-SH Team
# Version: 1.0

## Token Definitions
TOKEN NUMBER : \d+  (example: 42)  # Numbers
TOKEN OP : [+\-*/%^]  (example: +)  # Operators
TOKEN LPAREN : \(  (example: ()  # Left parenthesis
TOKEN RPAREN : \)  (example: ))  # Right parenthesis

## Grammar Rules
expr -> term  # Single term  -> evalTerm
expr -> expr OP term  # Binary operation  -> binaryOp(evalExpr, OP, evalTerm)
term -> NUMBER  # Number literal  -> parseNumber
term -> LPAREN expr RPAREN  # Parenthesized expression  -> evalExpr
term -> function  # Function call  -> callFunction
function -> func_name LPAREN args RPAREN  # Function  -> callFunction

## Built-in Functions
FUNC sin(angle)  # Sine function
    math.sin(angle)
FUNC cos(angle)  # Cosine function
    math.cos(angle)
FUNC sqrt(value)  # Square root
    math.sqrt(value)

## Runtime Configuration
SANDBOX enabled
MAX_TIME 10 seconds
MAX_MEMORY 5 MB
